# Spec 0035 — Materials & Library remaining gaps: editable categories, full-surface ribbon bays, dispersive ρ/μ, sample & material-editor polish

Full spec authored from the operator's preliminary spec
`specs/0033/.manual/010-remaining-gaps-and-additions-preliminary-spec.md`. It
closes the gaps left open after the 0033 cycle (G1, G2, G4, G5, G10, G14.3–G14.5,
plus the G6 presentation polish and two 0033 implementation gaps in the
material-editor preview). The ordered work lives in `.spec-jsonl`; this document
carries only the binding constraints, the contract table, and the per-part
orientation.

## 0. Binding constraints (every part)

0.1 **Elevate every primitive** (CLAUDE.md). New ids are single-case DUs with a
`.value` accessor plus `create`; enumerated conditions are named multi-case DUs
(no naked `bool`, no `enum`); every `*Error` case carries `reason : string` or a
typed payload; public functions have explicit concrete signatures. The category
change follows the existing elevated-id precedent `MaterialId`
(`…Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:27`) and `SampleId` (`…Domain/ElementId.fs:41`).

0.2 **No legacy, no fallback, no migration.** Categories change from the closed
multi-case union `MaterialCategory` (`…Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:67`) to an open
`CategoryId`-keyed set with NO compatibility shim: nothing is serialized, so
there is nothing to migrate, and every app start re-seeds the catalogue in
memory. The `UnsupportedComplexity` view-only fallback for dispersive ρ/μ
(`…Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:140,784,790`) and the
`NotAFiniteTermSum` / `SegmentNotLowerable` transcendental-rejection path
(`…Domain/DispersionModels.fs:505,666`; `MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:132,637`)
are REMOVED, not paralleled — the positive restatement is "every dispersion model
and every dispersive activity/magnetic entry is first-class, editable, and
drawable."

0.3 **All catalogue IO stays mocked and in-memory.** The new `CategoryProxy` is a
`[<ReferenceEquality>]` record of camelCase `Result`-returning functions built by
a `createInMemory` closing over a private mutable `Map`, exactly like
`SampleProxy.createInMemory` / `MaterialProxy.createInMemory`
(`…Domain/ElementId.fs:616,686`) and the `LibraryProxy` shape
(`…Domain/ElementId.fs:276`). This spec writes NO catalogue files to disk and
adds NO JSON-schema, versioning, or import/export work.

0.4 **UI is testable without a window** (CLAUDE.md WinForms-portability rule).
Every new editor surface is a pure Domain edit model plus a `Handlers`/message
record; behaviour is unit-tested in Domain, structure/interaction in the
`Avalonia.Headless` `ui-smoke` gate. Every new interactive control carries a
stable, intent-named `[<Literal>]` automation id in one `[<RequireQualifiedAccess>]`
ids module, following `MaterialEditorView` / `SampleEditorView`.

0.5 **Interpolated strings, never `sprintf`** (CLAUDE.md); four-space indent,
opening `{` on its own line, a space before every annotation colon, `camelCase`
record fields.

0.6 **Zero warnings from our code** (CLAUDE.md). Every slice MUST leave the build
free of any compiler warning originating in our code — F# `FS####` and MSBuild
warnings from our project configuration alike. The only exempt warnings are the
third-party NuGet advisories outside our control (`NU1701`, `NU1901`–`NU1904`).
In particular, if the build emits **`MSB3277`** (conflicting assembly versions)
from the WebView2 reference chain the Ui project carries
(`Microsoft.Web.WebView2`, `…Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj:176`, used by the
ChartHosts adapters, `:75,80`), it MUST be resolved at the reference level
(constrain or drop the offending reference) — never suppressed.

0.7 **Destructive-action / operator UX** (operator checklist, condensed — the new
Category editor is a sub-page reached from the Materials bay, with a destructive
Remove). The Category editor is opened by a `Categories…` verb on the Materials
bay (discoverability); every proxy verb is synchronous and in-memory, so there
are NO background jobs, NO progress UI, and NO pre-confirmation gate; after every
verb the editor re-queries `CategoryProxy` in the same MVU render pass (no manual
reload); Save/Cancel sit in one row with a visible gap and distinct
positive/negative styling; Remove is confirm-gated inline and has NO undo,
justified because the catalogue is in-memory session state a restart re-seeds; no
committable files are produced, so there is no `.gitignore` interaction. (The
spec-writer web pages' hidden-controls treatment does not apply: these are
desktop ribbon bays, not web pages.)

## Contract table (ids minted by the cycle)

| Placeholder | kind | declared in | role |
|---|---|---|---|
| `<STORE:CategoryProxy>` | proxy | OpticalConstructor.Domain | mutating category-catalogue write-seam |
| `<UICOMP:CategoryControls>` | component | OpticalConstructor.Controls | Category-manager control (domain-free) |
| `<UICOMP:CategoryEditorWindow>` | component | OpticalConstructor.TestWindows | category editor window |

