## Part A — Categories: an open, editable, Guid-keyed set (CRITICAL — land first)

### A.0 Problem statement

Today a material's category is a closed compile-time union
`MaterialCategory = Glass | Metal | Semiconductor | Crystal | Vacuum`
(`…Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:67`), stored directly on `MaterialEntry.category`
(`:119`) and `MaterialQuery.category` (`:368`), filtered by `byCategory` (`:146`)
and `byQuery` (`:417`), and hardcoded again in the material-editor create picker
(`…TestWindows/MaterialEditorView.fs:551,561`) and the Materials-bay category
facet (`…TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:1910,1915,1924,1934,2002`).
The operator's decision (preliminary spec §10) is that categories become an
**open, editable set** the user can add to, rename, and remove, keyed by a stable
`Guid` primary key with a renamable (and therefore translatable) display name.
This is the most load-bearing change in the spec — it re-types a domain field read
across the tree — so it lands first.

Recorded decisions (from the operator, preliminary spec §10):

- **Categories are data, not a union.** `MaterialCategory` becomes a small record
  `{ id : CategoryId; name : string; visibility : CategoryVisibility; origin :
  CategoryOrigin }` in a runtime catalogue; `MaterialEntry.category` and
  `MaterialQuery.category` reference the **`CategoryId`** primary key (a rename is
  one edit, never a sweep). The display name resolves through the catalogue by id.
- **Vacuum is a special built-in category, hidden from the create picker.** A real
  `BuiltInCategory` category the single seeded vacuum material
  (`…Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:314`) references, but never offered when creating a
  NEW material — modelled by `CategoryVisibility = SelectableOnCreate |
  HiddenOnCreate` (never a naked `bool`), Vacuum being `HiddenOnCreate`.
- **Built-ins are renamable but not removable; user categories are removable
  subject to a reference hard-block.** `CategoryOrigin = BuiltInCategory |
  UserCategory`. The Guid is the identity, so even a built-in's display label may
  change/translate; only removal is blocked for built-ins.
- **Removal never cascades.** `CategoryProxy.removeCategory` HARD-BLOCKS with a
  typed `CategoryStillReferenced` while any `MaterialEntry.category` names it —
  mirroring `MaterialProxy.removeMaterial`'s `MaterialStillReferenced` hard-block
  (`…Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:135`; assembled in `ElementId.fs:715`) — and
  refuses a built-in with `BuiltInNotRemovable`. The referencing lookup is a
  `materialsReferencingCategory` seam over the live materials store, exactly as
  `samplesReferencing` feeds material removal today (`…Domain/ElementId.fs:740`).

### A.1 Seeded catalogue and re-pointing

The current five categories seed with FIXED literal Guids (deterministic tests),
mirroring `MaterialLibrary.MaterialIds` (`…Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:51`): Glass,
Metal, Semiconductor, Crystal as `BuiltInCategory` / `SelectableOnCreate`, and
Vacuum as `BuiltInCategory` / `HiddenOnCreate`. Re-seed every
`MaterialEntry.category` (`…Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:252` onward) to the matching
seeded `CategoryId`, and re-express `byCategory` / `byQuery` as `CategoryId`
filters. The create picker (`MaterialEditorView.categoryRow`) offers only
`SelectableOnCreate` categories (Vacuum removed — not greyed); the Materials-bay
facet (`TableAndElementRotationView.materialCategories` / `…Code` / `…Label` /
`…OfCode`, `:1910`) is driven by the catalogue, its option code the `CategoryId`
Guid string and its label the category `name`, and it MAY still list a
`HiddenOnCreate` category that some entry uses so such entries stay filterable.

### A.2 The mutating category proxy and the manager surface

`<STORE:CategoryProxy>` is the mutating write-seam: `listCategories`,
`addCategory` (rejects a duplicate id), `updateCategory` (rename; rejects an
unknown id), `removeCategory` (the hard-block above). `CategoryError` carries
`UnknownCategoryId`, `DuplicateCategoryId`, `CategoryStillReferenced`,
`BuiltInNotRemovable`, and `InvalidCategory` (blank name), each with a `reason`.
`<UICOMP:CategoryControls>` is the domain-free manager control (the
`LibraryControls` shape) over a pure `CategoryEditor` Domain edit model (Add mints
`CategoryId.create ()` and a `UserCategory` / `SelectableOnCreate` row; Rename
edits `name`; Remove is confirm-gated and surfaces the typed block), and
`<UICOMP:CategoryEditorWindow>` hosts it in `OpticalConstructor.TestWindows`
beside the existing editor windows, launched by the Materials-bay `Categories…`
verb.

**Translation note (positive scope).** The mutable `name` field is what a future
per-locale name table would populate; wiring `Localization` is NOT this spec — the
data model only stops blocking it.

