## Part B — Ribbon hosting: single active pane, full-surface bays, last-two ordering

### B.0 Problem statement

`Ribbon.view` renders EVERY bay's content pane in one vertical `StackPanel` with
`IsVisible` toggles (`…Controls/Ribbon.fs:90,95-103`), and the module comment there
(`:84-89`) records why: swapping one shared content node between two different
controls makes FuncUI recycle a styled, named control across bays. That coupling
is exactly why moving the Library bay to the end regressed its sample-row layout
last cycle, so the "Details stays LAST" pin and the deferred reorder still stand
(`…TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:235-239`).

Two changes land together, the hosting fix first:

- **Order-independent hosting.** Make `Ribbon.view` host only the ACTIVE bay's
  content in a single stable, keyed content slot (keyed so FuncUI never recycles a
  styled/named control across bays — the hazard the all-panes design was avoiding).
  Once pane hosting is order-independent, reordering is safe.
- **Full-surface bays.** A bay declares its content mode as a two-case DU (never a
  `bool`): a table bay keeps the canvas plus its pan/zoom/rotate gestures; a
  full-surface bay replaces the canvas area entirely with the bay's own content.
  `mainView` (`…TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:2281`) wires the table
  canvas and pointer/wheel handlers ONLY for a table bay; the Materials and Library
  bays become full-surface. With hosting order-independent, make **Materials and
  Library the last two** bays in `mainBays` (`:2265`) and `BayNames.all` (`:239`),
  retiring the Details-LAST pin.

