## Part C — Dispersive gyration ρ and Polder μ editing

### C.0 Problem statement

`MaterialComplexityEditor.ofComplexity` returns the typed `UnsupportedComplexity`
for a formula-valued `RhoWithDispValue` / `MuWithDispValue`
(`…Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:784,790`), so such an entry opens view-only;
the edit state carries only the CONSTANT gyration (`gyration : GyrationClass<RhoValue>`,
`:117`) and Polder (`polder : PolderValue<MuValue>`, `:123`), and `toComplexity`
builds only the `RhoWithoutDispValue` / `MuWithoutDispValue` constant cases
(`:713,718`). The engine assembly for the dispersive cases already exists and is
UNCHANGED by this spec: `RhoWithDispValue.toRhoWithDisp` evaluates each component's
`DispersionFormula` per wavelength (`…OpticalProperties/Active.fs:152`), and
`MuWithDispValue.toMuWithDisp` does the same for the Polder tensor
(`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:644`). Only the EDITOR must lift the func-valued
data.

Extend both rungs to a **Constant vs Dispersive** sub-branch, mirroring the eps
ladder: each symmetry-allowed gyration component (the components
`gyrationComponents` already exposes, `…Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:385`)
and each Polder component becomes a `DispersionFormula` edited through the SAME
`DispersionModels.modelParameters` + raw `SumOfTerms` coefficient surface built in
0033 (`…Domain/DispersionModels.fs:291`). The edit state generalises so unchecking
Dispersive restores the constant losslessly (the ladder's existing lossless
discipline); `toComplexity` builds `RhoWithDispValue` / `MuWithDispValue` under the
sub-toggle, and `ofComplexity` seeds from a dispersive ρ / μ — the
`UnsupportedComplexity` case is deleted (§0.2).

