## Part D — Sample-editor polish

### D.0 Problem statement

Three independent sample-editor gaps (preliminary spec §7):

- **Empty-sample validation (G14.5).** `validateSample` checks the name only
  (`…Domain/ElementId.fs:596`). A sample with **no films AND no substrate** is
  structurally empty and MUST be refused on save with the typed `InvalidSample`
  (add the structure-content rule beside the name rule). The existing tests that
  save a structurally-empty sample are updated to add content.
- **Searchable material picker (G14.3).** The picker in
  `SampleEditorView.materialRow` (`…TestWindows/SampleEditorView.fs:647`) is a flat
  snapshot of `MaterialProxy.listMaterials`. Add a search box plus a category facet
  (mirroring the Materials bay, catalogue-driven), filtering the resolved list; the
  by-`MaterialId` selection contract (`ChooseMaterial of MaterialId`, `:190`) is
  kept.
- **Distinct *Make multilayer* (G14.4).** `SmpAdd` and `SmpMakeMultilayer` both
  open a blank editor today (`…TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:428,855`).
  Give `SmpMakeMultilayer` a launcher path that opens a NEW sample pre-seeded with a
  foldable starter period (a 2-layer `Repeated` cell ready for the K-stepper over
  `SampleStackEditor`, `…Domain/SampleStackEditor.fs:79`), distinct from the blank
  `Add`; extend the editor `init` with a "new-with-seed `SampleStructure`" path
  (not a `Some existing`, which means update-in-place) so Save still mints a fresh
  `SampleId`.

---

## Part E — Material-editor dispersion preview & transcendental models

### E.0 Problem statement

Three material-editor fixes (preliminary spec §8) — two are 0033 implementation
gaps, one is presentation polish.

- **Transcendental models are not usable in a dispersive segment today (0033
  implementation gap).** `DispersionModels.toEpsAxis` returns
  `Error (NotAFiniteTermSum _)` for Tauc–Lorentz, Gaussian, Forouhi–Bloomer and
  Brendel–Bormann (`…Domain/DispersionModels.fs:666-673`), so a dispersive segment
  carrying one fails `MaterialComplexityEditor.toComplexity` with
  `SegmentNotLowerable` (`:634,699,132`) — no properties, no chart, no save. Yet
  these models evaluate perfectly: `DispersionModels.evaluate` returns
  `WaveLength -> ComplexRefractionIndex` for every model
  (`…Domain/DispersionModels.fs:486`), and `toOpticalProperties` already wraps that
  closure for them (`:716`). Make them first-class in a dispersive segment: the core
  per-axis `EpsAxisDispersion` (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:306`) gains a case
  representing an **evaluated-directly** model whose `complexIndex` routes through
  `evaluate`; `toEpsAxis` lowers the four to it instead of erroring, and the editor
  stops surfacing `SegmentNotLowerable`. The finite-term models keep lowering to
  `RealNK` / `ComplexEps` (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:307-308`) exactly as
  today; only the transcendental four take the evaluated route.

  Two constraints bound HOW the new case is shaped, and the step's `how_to` commits
  to them:

  1. **Layering.** The core `Berreman.Dispersion` module cannot reference the
     Domain's `DispersionModel`, so the new case carries the evaluation the way the
     engine's own `EpsWithDisp of (WaveLength -> Eps)` case in the SAME file already
     does (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:11-12`) — a `WaveLength ->
     ComplexRefractionIndex` closure, built by `toEpsAxis` from the Domain's
     `evaluate`. The `EvaluatedModel of DispersionModel` shape the preliminary spec
     sketched is not buildable (it would invert the project layering); this is the
     resolved form.
  2. **Equality.** A function-typed union case removes F# structural equality
     type-wide, which the existing `Assert.Equal(model, back)` and
     `Assert.Equal(Ok axis, toEpsAxis model)` tests depend on
     (`…OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs:121,349`). So
     `EpsAxisDispersion` MUST keep supporting equality — a `[<CustomEquality>]`
     whose `RealNK` / `ComplexEps` data cases compare structurally and whose
     evaluated case compares by closure reference — so that `DispersionModel`,
     `EpsWithDispValue` and `MaterialComplexity` keep the equality those tests use.

  The transcendental round-trip acceptance is by SAMPLED n/k (the lowered case's
  `complexIndex` equals `DispersionModels.evaluate` across a wavelength grid), NOT
  structural `=` on the closure.

- **Reuse the shared chart control for the n/k preview (0033 implementation gap).**
  The editor's live n/k preview and the Materials-bay View panel both render through
  a primitive hand-rolled FuncUI canvas (`NkDispersionChart.inlineCanvas`,
  `…TestWindows/NkDispersionChart.fs:108`; used at
  `…TestWindows/MaterialEditorView.fs:856`) — it neither looks nor behaves like the
  experiment chart. 0033 Part D already REAL-MOVED the shared ScottPlot chart into
  `OpticalConstructor.Controls` with the dual n-left / k-right Y axes
  (`…Controls/ExperimentChart.fs`, `…Controls/ChartWindow.fs`), but only as the
  pop-out window (`ChartWindow.fs:11-19`); the editor never embedded it. Expose an
  inline/embeddable form of that dual-axis ScottPlot control and embed it as the
  editor preview and the Materials View panel, so a dispersion curve here is the
  experiment chart; delete `NkDispersionChart.inlineCanvas`. The pure chart-model
  builder `NkDispersionChart.nkDispersionChart` (`:55`) is reused unchanged. Every
  model kind — including the four transcendental — draws n and k. The embedded
  control MUST render under the headless `ui-smoke` frame without throwing so the
  gate stays green.

- **Constant-vs-Dispersive presentation (G6).** The primary eps branch is a sticky
  `Dispersive` toggle ("off = constant n, k", `…TestWindows/MaterialEditorView.fs:594,604`).
  Present it as two mutually-exclusive options (Constant / Dispersive) so the branch
  reads as a choice; update the `absorbingToggle` / `dispersiveToggle` acceptance
  tests (`:56,58`) to the two-option model. Cosmetic — the derived model is
  unchanged.

